 <details class="risk-guide"><summary>${x("info")} How risk priorities work</summary><div class="risk-guide-grid"><article><span class="priority-pill red">Red · priority check-in</span><p>No sessions in the latest snapshot plus two or more consecutive weekly zero snapshots, or a stop from at least two sessions last week / a prior average of at least two.</p></article><article><span class="priority-pill yellow">Yellow · personal check-in</span><p>A new zero week with visits in the last 30 days, a drop of at least two sessions from last week or 1.5 below the prior average, or declining Fringe attendance.</p></article><article><span class="priority-pill watch">Watch · monitor</span><p>Still attending, marked Fringe and below their membership target, with no stronger Red or Yellow signal. Unlimited memberships use a target of four sessions.</p></article><article><span class="priority-pill review">Review · missing context</span><p>Zero attendance without enough weekly history, or below-target attendance without the engagement label needed for Watch. Review these cases before choosing an outreach outcome.</p></article></div><p class="risk-guide-note"><strong>Attendance stages:</strong> Early warning = first zero after recent attendance; At risk = two zero snapshots, a sharp stop or declining attendance; Disengaged = 3–4 zero snapshots; Long absence = 5–6; Extended absence = 7+. Monitoring and Needs context describe cases without a confirmed absence stage. Stages use up to eight saved weekly observations. Missing, suspended or ineligible historical slots break the run. Archived weekly summaries are observations, not a verified day-by-day absence record. Existing reports retain their saved history until reimported. Outreach notes and exemptions stay separate.</p><p class="risk-guide-note"><strong>Attendance bands are different:</strong> 0 = Critical; 1 = At Risk; 2 = Low; 3 = Okay; 4+ = Good. Outreach priority also considers history and membership target. The first matching rule wins: Red, then Yellow, then Watch. Missing snapshots are not counted as zero. Current suspensions are held out of outreach.</p><p class="risk-guide-note"><strong>Missing history:</strong> CSV imports keep missing snapshots unknown and flag unresolved cases as Review. They do not assume a Red risk or invent a Fringe engagement label.</p><p class="risk-guide-note">Imported reports supply these priorities; CSV imports calculate them from the selected cutoff and saved weekly attendance. Team notes change outreach status and temporary exemptions; they do not change the recorded risk category.</p></details>
